Werewolf Linux playground: a hardened, image-based Linux to try out.
The system is a read-only image; only /data keeps what you write.

NOTE: This environment is locked-down by default!
- / is read-only
- Only signed binaries execute
- Processes are controlled by seccomp and Landlock
- Application firewalling is in place

If you find a way to run arbitrary code - open an issue!

Useful commands:
- /usr/lib/werewolf/posture: security checks!
- /usr/lib/werewolf/slot-update: install updated software (A/B)
